"**par défaut** : Construire(build) pour l'architecture qui correspond à la "
"plate-forme hôte."

#: development/compiling/introduction_to_the_buildsystem.rst:175
msgid ""
"This flag appends ``.32`` or ``.64`` suffixes to resulting binaries when "
"relevant. If ``bits=default`` is used, the suffix will match the detected "
"architecture."
msgstr ""
"Ce signal concatène les suffixes ``.32`` ou ``.64`` au binaires obtenus si "
"nécessaire. Si ``bits=default`` est utilisé, le suffixe correspondra à "
"l'architecture détectée."

#: development/compiling/introduction_to_the_buildsystem.rst:180
msgid "Custom modules"
msgstr "Modules personnalisées"

#: development/compiling/introduction_to_the_buildsystem.rst:182
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"It's possible to compile modules residing outside of Rebel Engine's "
"directory tree, along with the built-in modules."
msgstr ""
"Il est possible de compiler des modules résidant à l’extérieur de l’arbre de "
"répertoire de Godot, en même temps que les modules intégrés."

#: development/compiling/introduction_to_the_buildsystem.rst:185
msgid ""
"A ``custom_modules`` build option can be passed to the command line before "
"compiling. The option represents a comma-separated list of directory paths "
"containing a collection of independent C++ modules that can be seen as C++ "
"packages, just like the built-in ``modules/`` directory."
msgstr ""
