#: development/editor/editor_style_guide.rst:2
msgid "Editor style guide"
msgstr "Guide de style de l'éditeur"

#: development/editor/editor_style_guide.rst:7
#, fuzzy
msgid "Thanks for your interest in contributing to the Rebel Editor!"
msgstr "Merci de votre intérêt à la contribution à l'éditeur de Godot !"

#: development/editor/editor_style_guide.rst:9
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"This page describes the grammar and writing style used throughout the Rebel "
"Editor. Following this style guide will help your contribution get merged "
"faster since there will be fewer review steps required."
msgstr ""
"Cette page décrit la grammaire et le style d'écriture utilisés dans "
"l'éditeur Godot. Suivre ce guide de style, aidera votre contribution a être "
"fusionnée plus rapidement, car les étapes de révision seront moins "
"nombreuses."

#: development/editor/editor_style_guide.rst:14
msgid "Writing style"
msgstr "Style d'écriture"

#: development/editor/editor_style_guide.rst:16
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"**Write messages (errors, warnings, …) as full sentences.** They should "
"start with an uppercase letter and end with a period."
msgstr ""
"**Écrivez les messages (erreurs, avertissements, ...) sous forme de phrases "
"complètes** Elles doivent commencer par une lettre majuscule et se terminer "
"par un point."

#: development/editor/editor_style_guide.rst:18
msgid ""
"**Try to keep sentences short.** This makes it more likely that their "
"translations will be short as well, which is a good thing to avoid UI bugs."
msgstr ""
"**Essayez de garder les phrases courtes.** Cela rend plus probable que leurs "
"traductions soient également courtes, ce qui est une bonne chose pour éviter "
"les bogues de l'interface utilisateur."

#: development/editor/editor_style_guide.rst:20
msgid ""
"**Use contractions.** For example, use \"isn't\" instead of \"is not\". An "
"exception to this rule can be made when you specifically want to emphasize "
"one of the contraction's words."
msgstr ""
"**Utilisez des contractions.** Par exemple, utilisez \"isn't\" au lieu de "
"\"is not\". Une exception à cette règle peut être faite lorsque vous "
"souhaitez spécifiquement souligner l'un des mots de la contraction."

#: development/editor/editor_style_guide.rst:23
msgid ""
"**Use double quotes in messages** (``\"\"``) instead of single quotes "
"(``''``). Double quotes should be used to quote user input, file paths and "
"possibly other things depending on the context."
msgstr ""
"**Utilisez des guillemets doubles dans les messages** (``\"\"``) au lieu de "
"guillemets simples (``''``). Les guillemets doubles doivent être utilisés "
"pour citer les entrées de l'utilisateur, les chemins d'accès aux fichiers et "
"éventuellement d'autres choses selon le contexte."

#: development/editor/editor_style_guide.rst:29
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Try to follow the :doc:`/contributing/docs_writing_guidelines` in addition "
"to the guidelines outlined above."
msgstr ""
"Essayez de suivre les lignes directrices :ref:`doc_docs_writing_guidelines` "
"en plus des lignes directrices décrites ci-dessus."

#: development/editor/editor_style_guide.rst:33
msgid "Button and menu texts"
msgstr "Textes des boutons et des menus"

#: development/editor/editor_style_guide.rst:35
msgid "Capitalize text in buttons and menu actions:"
msgstr "Mettez le texte en majuscule dans les boutons et les actions de menu :"

#: development/editor/editor_style_guide.rst:37
msgid "**Good:** *Open Editor Data Folder*"
msgstr "**Bien :** *Open Editor Data Folder*"

#: development/editor/editor_style_guide.rst:38
msgid "**Bad:** *Open editor data folder*"
msgstr "**Mauvais :** *Open editor data folder*"

#: development/editor/editor_style_guide.rst:40
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"If a menu action opens a modal dialog, suffix it with an ellipsis (``…``)."
msgstr ""
"Si une action de menu ouvre un dialogue modal, suffixez-le par une ellipse "
"(``...``)."

#: development/editor/editor_style_guide.rst:42
#, fuzzy
msgid "**Good:** *Editor Settings…*"
msgstr "**Bon :** *Editor Settings...*"

#: development/editor/editor_style_guide.rst:43
msgid "**Bad:** *Editor Settings*"
msgstr "**Mauvais :** *Editor Settings*"

#: development/editor/editor_style_guide.rst:46
msgid "Inspector sections"
msgstr "Sections de l'inspecteur"

#: development/editor/editor_style_guide.rst:48
msgid ""
"In general, don't create sections that contain less than 3 items. Sections "
"that contain few items make it difficult to navigate the inspector, while "
"missing the benefits of using sections such as folding."
msgstr ""
"En général, ne créez pas de sections qui contiennent moins de 3 éléments. "
"Les sections qui contiennent peu d'éléments rendent la navigation dans "
"l'inspecteur difficile, tout en ne bénéficiant pas des avantages de "
"l'utilisation de sections telles que le pliage."

#: development/editor/editor_style_guide.rst:52
msgid ""
"There are some valid exceptions for this, such as material features in :ref:"
"`class_SpatialMaterial`."
msgstr ""
"Il y a quelques exceptions valables, telles que les caractéristiques "
"matérielles dans :ref:`class_SpatialMaterial`."

#: development/editor/editor_style_guide.rst:55
msgid "This advice also applies to the Project Settings and Editor Settings."
msgstr ""
"Ces conseils s'appliquent également aux paramètres du projet et de l'éditeur."

#: development/editor/editor_style_guide.rst:58
msgid "Inspector performance hints"
msgstr "Indices de performance de l'inspecteur"

#: development/editor/editor_style_guide.rst:60
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Enum properties that noticeably impact performance should have a performance "
"hint associated. The hint should refer to the *absolute* performance impact, "
"rather than being relative to the other options provided in the enum. Here "
"are some examples taken from the Rebel Editor:"
msgstr ""
"Les propriétés énumérées qui ont un impact notable sur les performances "
"devrait être associé à un indice de performance. L'indice doit faire "
"référence à l'impact *absolu* sur les performances, plutôt que d'être "
"relatif aux autres options fournies dans l'énumération. Voici quelques "
"exemples tirés de l'éditeur Godot :"

#: development/editor/editor_style_guide.rst:65
msgid "**Screen-space antialiasing:** *Disabled (Fastest), FXAA (Fast)*"
msgstr "**Screen-space antialiasing:** *Disabled (Fastest), FXAA (Fast)*"

#: development/editor/editor_style_guide.rst:66
msgid ""
"**MSAA quality:** *Disabled (Fastest), 2x (Fast), 4x (Average), 8x (Slow), "
"16x (Slower)*"
msgstr ""
"**MSAA quality:** *Disabled (Fastest), 2x (Fast), 4x (Average), 8x (Slow), "
"16x (Slower)*"

#: development/editor/editor_style_guide.rst:68
msgid ""
"**DirectionalLight mode:** *Orthogonal (Fast), PSSM 2 Splits (Average), PSSM "
"4 Splits (Slow)*"
msgstr ""
"**DirectionalLight mode:** *Orthogonal (Fast), PSSM 2 Splits (Average), PSSM "
"4 Splits (Slow)*"

#: development/editor/editor_style_guide.rst:71
msgid ""
"For consistency, try to stick to the terms below (from fastest to slowest):"
msgstr ""
"Par souci de cohérence, essayez de vous en tenir aux termes ci-dessous (de "
"fastest à slowest) :"

#: development/editor/editor_style_guide.rst:73
msgid "*Fastest, Faster, Fast, Average, Slow, Slower, Slowest*"
msgstr "*Fastest, Faster, Fast, Average, Slow, Slower, Slowest*"

#: development/editor/editor_style_guide.rst:75
msgid ""
"Their usage doesn't have to be contiguous. For example, you can use only "
"\"Fast\" and \"Slow\" from the list above."
msgstr ""
"Leur utilisation n'a pas besoin d'être contiguë. Par exemple, vous pouvez "
"utiliser uniquement \"Fast\" et \"Slow\" dans la liste ci-dessus."

#: development/editor/editor_style_guide.rst:78
msgid ""
"If you're adding a new enum, its values should be ordered from the fastest "
"option to the slowest option."
msgstr ""
"Si vous ajoutez une nouvelle énumération, ses valeurs doivent être classées "
"de l'option la plus rapide à l'option la plus lente."

#: development/editor/editor_style_guide.rst:82
msgid "Tooltips"
msgstr "Info-bulles"

#: development/editor/editor_style_guide.rst:84
msgid ""
"Consider adding tooltips whenever the action performed by a button or menu "
"action isn't obvious. You can also provide additional context or highlight "
"caveats in the tooltip."
msgstr ""
"Envisagez d'ajouter des infobulles chaque fois que l'action effectuée par un "
"bouton ou une action de menu n'est pas évidente. Vous pouvez également "
"fournir un contexte supplémentaire ou mettre en évidence des avertissements "
"dans l'infobulle."

#: development/editor/editor_style_guide.rst:88
msgid ""
"You can do this by calling ``set_tooltip(TTR(\"Text here.\"))`` on the "
"Control-based node in question. If the tooltip is particularly long (more "
"than ~80 characters), wrap it over several lines by adding line breaks using "
"``\\n``."
msgstr ""
"Vous pouvez le faire en appelant ``set_tooltip(TTR(\"Text here.\"))`` sur le "
"nœud basé sur Control en question. Si l'info-bulle est particulièrement "
"longue (plus de ~80 caractères), vous pouvez l'encapsuler sur plusieurs "
"lignes en ajoutant des sauts de ligne en utilisant ``\\n``."

#: development/editor/editor_style_guide.rst:92
msgid ""
"Tooltips should follow the writing style described above. In addition to "
"this, use indicative mood instead of imperative mood:"
msgstr ""
"Les infobulles doivent suivre le style d'écriture décrit ci-dessus. En "
"outre, utilisez un ton indicatif au lieu d'un ton impératif :"

#: development/editor/editor_style_guide.rst:95
msgid "**Good:** *Computes global illumination for the selected GIProbe.*"
msgstr "**Bon :** *Computes global illumination for the selected GIProbe.*"

#: development/editor/editor_style_guide.rst:96
msgid "**Bad:** *Compute global illumination for the selected GIProbe.*"
msgstr "**Mauvais :** *Compute global illumination for the selected GIProbe.*"

