#: tutorials/shaders/your_first_shader/your_second_3d_shader.rst:55
msgid ""
"First let's set the color of the water. We do that by setting ``ALBEDO``."
msgstr ""
"Commençons par définir la couleur de l'eau. Nous le faisons en définissant "
"``ALBEDO``."

#: tutorials/shaders/your_first_shader/your_second_3d_shader.rst:57
msgid "``ALBEDO`` is a ``vec3`` that contains the color of the object."
msgstr "``ALBEDO`` est un ``vec3`` qui contient la couleur de l'objet."

#: tutorials/shaders/your_first_shader/your_second_3d_shader.rst:59
msgid "Let's set it to a nice shade of blue."
msgstr "Mettons une belle nuance de bleu."

#: tutorials/shaders/your_first_shader/your_second_3d_shader.rst:69
msgid ""
"We set it to a very dark shade of blue because most of the blueness of the "
"water will come from reflections from the sky."
msgstr ""
"Nous l'avons réglé sur une teinte de bleu très sombre car la plus grande "
